{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01X49vBqyCfbwsZMh2LtKrrY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system. Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose:** A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), single-user productivity system for J.C. Liechty â€” a markdown-backed task/project manager with no database and (one declared exception aside) no external dependencies, where plain-text markdown files are the source of truth.\n\n- **What it does (task management):** Tracks tasks and projects across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) through a full lifecycle â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” via an inbox-capture, dashboard, and weekly-review workflow.\n\n- **How you use it:** It ships a self-contained Python-stdlib web server (`anchor_gui.py`) that runs persistently as a Windows NSSM service on `http://localhost:8777`, generating an interactive browser dashboard that reads/writes the markdown directly. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same operations plus static-HTML generation, and a 5 AM scheduled health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) self-tests file integrity and every endpoint.\n\n- **R&D control surface (the larger half):** It layers a \"trio\" R&D cockpit on top â€” driving the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio per project. Through v2/v3/v4 it adds a session model with cached/validated summaries, a Grass-Catchers idea lane, deliverable pin/declare/launch-by-type, real ConPTY interactive terminals with per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, stage handoffs, ephemeral deliverable previews (hard-guarded off port 8777), and an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini). v4 \"Project Cockpit\" presents each lane as a status-lit tile expanding to an inline summary-over-terminal panel.\n\n- **What it ships (the declared deliverable):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” the running web application itself â€” is the pinned, declared deliverable of the project.\n\nNote: this summary is grounded in `CLAUDE.md` and the project anchors, not in re-reading the source â€” say the word if you want me to verify any specific claim against the code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e870915c-3b4c-46bc-b545-bcd60ba5529f","uuid":"90d85d1b-a62e-4d8e-b50d-70790be02e5e","request_id":"req_011Cc1JcMwzRM5VZGGqE29SF"}
